      ":question/problem": "Find $c\\cdot (a\\times b),$ if $a\\cdot ((-3b)\\times (-7c))=7.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we factor out the constants and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot ((-3b)\\times (-7c)) & =7 \\\\ (-3)\\cdot (-7)\\cdot [a\\cdot (b\\times c)] & =7 \\\\ a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we swap $a$ and $c$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot (b\\times a) & =-\\frac{1}{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand again we swap $a$ and $b$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot (a\\times b) & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
