      ":question/problem": "Find $b\\cdot (a\\times c),$ if $b\\times c=⟨2,5,1⟩$ and $a=⟨6,1,-9⟩.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we compute the triple scalar product \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨6,1,-9⟩\\cdot ⟨2,5,1⟩ \\\\  & =6\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 5+(-9)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =12+5-9 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we swap $a$ and $b$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b\\cdot (a\\times c)=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
