      ":question/problem": "Find $b\\cdot (c\\times a),$ if $b\\times c=⟨4,-1,6⟩$ and $a=⟨2,3,-1⟩.$\n\n$b\\cdot (c\\times a)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we compute the triple scalar product \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨2,3,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨4,-1,6⟩ \\\\  & =2\\cdot 4+3\\cdot (-1)+(-1)\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =8-3-6 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we swap $a$ and $b$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b\\cdot (a\\times c)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand again we swap $a$ and $c$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b\\cdot (c\\times a)=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
