      ":question/problem": "Find $c\\cdot (b\\times a)$, if $b\\times c=⟨3,-1,2⟩$ and $a=⟨4,-2,6⟩.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we compute the triple scalar product \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨4,-2,6⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-1,2⟩ \\\\  & =4\\cdot 3+(-2)\\cdot (-1)+6\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =12+2+12 \\\\  & =26.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we swap $a$ and $c$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot (b\\times a)=-26.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
